Agent-Fleet wire format — FROZEN
================================

Version 1. The header, frame layout, size classes, and message-type numbers below
are frozen. Any change requires a new `magic` and `version` plus a new revision of
this file; v1 decoders must keep rejecting unknown magic or version values.

This file is machine-checked by `crates/msgfmt` in the test
`frozen_wire_format_matches_the_checked_in_contract`. That test parses the
`key = value` lines, compares them to the live constants, then encodes a real
frame and asserts every header offset, the zero padding, the class size, and the
signature. Editing the constants without editing this file fails the test.

magic = 43320001
version = 1
header_len = 49
signature_len = 64
aead_tag_len = 16
max_payload = 3967
size_classes = 256,512,1024,4096

Header layout (little-endian)
-----------------------------
offset  size  field
0       4     magic: 43 32 00 01 ("C2", NUL, 0x01)
4       2     version: 1
6       1     message type: 1 heartbeat, 2 task, 3 result, 4 rotate,
              5 upgrade, 6 relay set, 7 mod set, 8 peer record
7       8     route tag
15      8     epoch (u64)
23      24    XChaCha20-Poly1305 nonce
47      2     payload length (u16): ciphertext length including the 16-byte AEAD tag

Frame layout
------------
[0 .. 49)                        header; authenticated as AEAD associated data and
                                 included in the signed region
[49 .. 49 + payload_len)         ciphertext
[49 + payload_len .. len - 64)   zero padding to the class size
[len - 64 .. len)                Ed25519 signature over [0 .. len - 64)

A frame length must be exactly one of the size classes above. Payload length is
bounded by `max_payload`; the smallest valid payload is `aead_tag_len`.
